#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The README's and the website's pictures, made again, in 4K (Ben,
2026-11-07: "a full collection of screenshots in light/dark and different
themes and make sure they cover all the different apps, features, agent
functionality etc"; 2026-11-16: "take new screenshots via olo agent
screens (use a high res screen to get 4k screenshots) of all the features
and apps").

  tools/dev/readme-shots [SCENE...]     (default: every scene)
  tools/dev/readme-shots --list         the scenes

An Agent Screen of its own (`olo-screen start readme --size 3840x2160
--scale 2`: a whole headless Olo desktop, Deskbar and Tracker's desktop
included), from this tree's release build (target/release/olo-screen, so
the screen runs the build's app_server and apps), with a runtime folder
of its own (none of the person's screens are seen or touched) and a
sample home folder (`fixture-home`, with some of Olo's wallpapers in its
Pictures: nothing of anyone's). Each scene sets the look it wants, opens
and places its windows through app_server's IPC (the screen's
OLO_SOCKET), drives them with olo-screen (keys, typing, clicks), waits
for them to settle and saves `docs/img/NAME.png`: 3840 × 2160 (or a
crop of it), lossless. Apps that would show this computer's own
(the journal, processes, devices, accounts) are left out or run on their
demo data. Look at every picture before committing it.

Build first: `jato build --release --workspace`, or picture a release's
own build (OLO_SHOTS_BUILD, below). Run with /usr/bin/python3 (it has
PIL).

What the pictures show is nobody's: each app runs on its demo (Rex's
hosts and agents, Token Pool's accounts, Calendar's and To-Do's month,
Phone's people, Telegram's chats, Weather's place, the Speed Test's
line, Doctor's findings, Kache's builds, the Installer's computer), the
Google accounts in Integrations are made up and taken for signed in
(`OLO_GOOGLE_ACCOUNTS`' file in the sample home, `OLO_PREFS_DEMO_GOOGLE=
signed`), and the desktop's disk has a name of the pictures' own
(`OLO_TRACKER_DEMO_VOLUME`). Deskbar is as a person's
(`OLO_DESKBAR_DEMO_PERSON=1`: on an agent's screen it shows no live
widgets). A picture of windows alone is cropped to them and a margin of
wallpaper (`shot_of`), clear of the desktop's icons and Deskbar. Apps
that can only show this computer's own (Activity Monitor's processes
and hardware, the Log Viewer's journal, OS Updates' packages) have no
picture.

In the environment:
  OLO_SHOTS_BUILD=DIR       the build pictured (default target/release)
  OLO_SHOTS_OUT=DIR         where the pictures go (default docs/img)
  OLO_SHOTS_EMOJI_FONT=FILE an emoji font for the screen, where the
                            computer has none (a server)
  OLO_SHOTS_SOFTWARE=1      draw on the processors (by itself where
                            there is no GPU)
"""

